#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pikemen,†1]]1. Pikemen"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:103
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:142
msgid ""
"The pike is the traditional weapon of the mercenaries of Tilea. Twice as "
"long as a spear and even longer than a cavalryman’s lance this is a truly "
"fearsome although rather unwieldy weapon. Due to this Pikemen never benefit "
"from defended or fortified status when in dense terrain (even partially) or "
"on fortress walls etc. They still count as defended on higher ground or "
"behind low obstacles as usual.  Pikemen count as defended against cavalry or "
"chariots charging to their front, except when the Pikemen are in dense "
"terrain.  This bonus only applies in the first combat round of an engagement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:110
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Pikemen stands may only give or receive support by other infantry or Pikemen "
"stands that are facing the same direction and touching their flank with the "
"whole of their own flank. Any support behind or in front of Pikemen stand is "
"not allowed. In all other respects they count as infantry (movement/pursuit "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dogs-of-war.adoc:113
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/regiments-of-renown.adoc:152
msgid ""
"Pikemen are based as cavalry – i.e. the models are orientated towards the "
"narrow edge of the base."
msgstr ""

